# -*- coding: utf-8 -*-
"""
MASTER clock alignment pipeline (ENGLISH)

Key rule:
  - Video + Fiber DEFINE the MASTER clock (after the same TRIM).
  - MedPC is aligned AFTERWARDS to MASTER using a ONE-WAY affine transform:
        MASTER_time ≈ a * MedPC_time + b
  - Video is NEVER warped to MedPC.
  - Fiber is NEVER warped to MedPC.

Extras you asked for:
  1) Leave-one-anchor-out (LOO) robustness:
     - We try dropping each manual anchor (one at a time),
       run monotonic DP matching + affine fit on the remaining anchors,
       score the solution, and pick the best scenario.
     - The "best" scenario determines which first element (anchor) is excluded.

  2) Tiny progress bar (console) + partial results printed to screen:
     - We print a NEAREST-candidates table similar to your example.
     - We print the chosen dropped anchor (if any), affine (a,b), match stats, and AUC stats.

Outputs (in root/outputs):
  - alignment_report.csv              : matched anchors ↔ MedPC events (+ self_administrator)
  - medpc_events_master.csv           : all MedPC events with MASTER times
  - selected_clips_manifest.csv       : clip list (ranked by peak Z)
  - fiber_master.parquet / csv        : prepared fiber on MASTER axis
  - peri_event_summary.npz            : mean/SEM/AUC etc.
  - bootstrap_affine_ab.csv           : bootstrap distribution of (a,b) (if enough matches)
  - run_meta.json                     : run metadata including dropped anchor
"""

